{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 634 -First 145; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1234 -First 24; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1426 -First 36; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1629 -First 22; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 2184 -First 18; Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-Object -Skip 643 -First 25; Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1358 -First 20; Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1534 -First 35'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 634 -First 145; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1234 -First 24; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1426 -First 36; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1629 -First 22; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 2184 -First 18; Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-Object -Skip 643 -First 25; Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1358 -First 20; Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1534 -First 35'","aggregated_output":"[requirement.SR-148]\r\ntitle = \"Autonomous loop work selection: what it derives from, and in what order\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-025\", \"SN-029\", \"SN-027\", \"SN-006\", \"SN-008\", \"SN-010\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-05\", \"B-09\", \"B-10\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"The delivered loop content shall select exactly one work item for each assignment an unattended run admits from the repository's tracked registries and git history alone, in this order: ready adjudication rows first, as a stable partition applied at admission rather than by renumbering the ruled rank table; then unresolved handback records; then the earliest incomplete spine tier in SN-to-SR-to-LLR-to-TC order; then implementation work after test-case layout is complete — with the eligible set and its order deterministic, an item whose declared safety, policy or plan-mode inputs are missing, undeclared or contradictory failing closed for that item alone, human holds applied only from the declared approval level, nothing admitted past a human-held stop, no prose surface and no predefined track in the derivation, no hand-curated next-work or run-phase pointer surface shipped for any live instruction or executable surface to read, write, validate, generate or link, and the status surface a session reads generated and freshness-gated rather than hand-copied.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Without one precedence rule, the same repository can resume into implementation while returned obligations or prerequisite requirement tiers remain unresolved. That produces work against stale intent and makes repeated resumes select different next actions. A recorded selection class, source record and hold decision provide replayable evidence of the choice. ONE SR PER (need, property): the loop's work-selection invariant — what the next work derives from, in what order, and that no hand-curated pointer surface participates in it — is stated here and nowhere else, so no second row can drift from it. An explicit three-way partition was rejected: the partition already existed textually and still produced duplicated acceptance. The no-pointer obligation is stated for a migrated repository as well as a fresh scaffold, and the migrated half is the one that matters most: a fresh scaffold never had the files to keep, while an upgraded repository can retain the retired authority files and still pass. Fan-out re-stamp: this row states one decision — what an unattended run's next work derives from and in what order — and its children are the successive stages of that one selection, not separable contracts; the width is the deliberate consolidation of three rows that stated the same invariant into one, so re-splitting to satisfy the bound would restore the duplication the consolidation removed.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A ready adjudication row admits ahead of every other class, the ruled rank table unchanged (--explain still reports it) and non-adjudication rows keeping their relative order; an unresolved handback is selected before spine or implementation work, and processing it either resolves the record or mints a provenance-linked successor exactly once or names an already-open work item that supersedes the closed work item as its successor; with no unresolved handback, only the earliest incomplete spine tier is eligible; implementation work is ineligible while any required test case remains unlaid; at human_approval_through = 0 no spine tier produces a human hold, each higher level holds exactly its documented cumulative tiers, and a human-held attestation still drains and surfaces with the adjudication row waiting behind the stop; every selection records the chosen class, source identifier and hold decision. Two resumes over the same tracked state select the same eligible set in the same order; an item with missing or contradictory declared inputs is excluded with a stated reason while disjoint classified work stays eligible; no prose surface participates in the derivation; the ordering and exclusion reasons are exposed for replay. A fresh scaffold ships no next-wi/run-phase pointer and is parallel-by-default; no live instruction or executable surface reads, writes, validates, generates or links such a pointer; a build-out lane's phase resolves from its branch name with no pointer file; an upgraded or resynced repository that once carried such a pointer carries neither pointer file after the migration and no live dependency on either survives, so the deletion holds for a migrated repository and not only for a fresh scaffold; the status snapshot regenerates mechanically and its freshness is gated.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"S\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-006\"]\r\naspect = \"unattended-loop\"\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-149]\r\ntitle = \"Retired-vocabulary refusal in authored surfaces\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-010\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-09\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"MAINTAINER\"]\r\nrequirement = \"The harness shall report every occurrence of a retired process tag in a live authored surface — naming the file and line and the vocabulary that replaces it, at a severity that warns by default and fails under --strict — reporting none in a declared historical, generated or attestation-quoting surface, nor in a line or file marked as a declaration site.\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-010 (a reader can navigate the documentation and trust it: navigable and honest). This check is a CONDITION of the vocabulary conversion rather than a follow-up, on measured evidence: an earlier sweep removed a retired-tag construct from this repo's own open-items registry and it REGENERATED within days, caught only by an audit. A ~2,500-edit conversion held in place by attention is a conversion that comes undone. The carve-outs are as load-bearing as the rule: history is not rewritten and an attestation is never re-worded, because a swept sign-off makes a signed record claim something was signed that was not. C-MNT-3 gives every declared vocabulary value exactly one normative definition in one home; a retired tag surviving in a live authored surface is a second, contradictory definition of the same word, which is why the earlier sweep regenerated within days when only attention held it.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A planted retired tag in a live authored file is reported with its path and line, at exit 0 under the default severity and exit 1 under --strict; a file under any declared carve-out class (archive, the project log, attestation briefs, closed and cancelled work-item specs, generated surfaces) reports nothing, including at arbitrary depth; a line carrying the allow marker or a file carrying the allow-file marker reports nothing; and the word \"gate\" used to mean a check that can fail reports nothing.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"S\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\ncoincident = \"\"\"The need asks that a reader can trust the documentation: navigable and honest. A retired process tag surviving in a live authored surface names a step by a word the process no longer defines, a second and contradictory definition of it; each one reported with its file, line and the vocabulary that replaces it, warned by default and failing under --strict, while history, generated surfaces and attestation quotes are left as written, is that honesty held by the harness's own check rather than by attention.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-150]\r\ntitle = \"Stakeholder-need cells stay in stakeholder language\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-033\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-09\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"PRODUCT-FITNESS\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"The harness shall report each stakeholder-need `need` cell that contains an internal path, an implementation-only identifier or a process citation, naming the row and the offending phrase — at a severity that warns by default and fails only under --strict, exempting a name declared on a reviewed exception list that ships empty (a name that is itself a user-facing interface belongs in a need), and reporting nothing for acceptance or engineering-requirement cells, which SN-033 exempts by its own text.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-033 — its approved acceptance commissions exactly this check, and until this row it did not exist. The need tier was measured clean when this landed (0 of 27 cells), and the row sits deliberately AHEAD of the SR re-tier's churn: locking the clean state in costs one warn-first step now; trusting a large re-statement pass not to dirty it costs an audit later. Warn-first is the ruled posture, not a softness — a form heuristic over approved stakeholder prose must not gate without an owner ruling, and that ruling has not been made.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A need cell planted with an internal path, an implementation-only identifier and a process citation is reported, naming the row and each offending phrase separately rather than the row alone; the report leaves the run passing by default and failing under the declared strict mode, which is the whole of the severity claim; a token on the reviewed exception list is not reported, and that list ships empty; the same three tokens planted in an acceptance or engineering-requirement cell are not reported, because the need governs the need cell only; and the live need registry reports zero findings.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"S\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\ncoincident = \"\"\"The need asks for a stakeholder recognizing their outcome in each need; each offending phrase reported with its row is what the author needs to fix it, and the report is the check's whole promise.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-151]\r\ntitle = \"Hosted CI runs the declared bar per trigger\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-005\", \"SN-004\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"CONSISTENCY\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"The shipped reference CI workflow shall invoke, for each declared hosted trigger (push, pull request, schedule) across its declared OS x Python matrix, the same documented harness entry point at the tier the declared moment-to-tier table assigns to that moment.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-005 — one definition of passing per moment, its acceptance's own words — and SN-004. The obligation existed but had no row of its own: it rode SR-019's acceptance cell (census finding F1). Attributed to B-05, the delivered package, on the DESIGN-CONTROL reading: what this system delivers is a METHOD for a CI runner to invoke, and it holds no design authority over whether an external runner honours the configuration it is handed — so the obligation this row can actually carry is a property of the shipped workflow file, not of a hosted trigger arriving. The frame draws the runner as a party of its own, hosted CI (EXT-007), whose hosted run of the declared bar crosses at B-11: being outside design control is what makes it external, not a reason to leave it undrawn, and it is why this row constrains the shipped workflow rather than the runner's behaviour. Stated artifact-shaped per §1R.6: the job files are a standing thing whose declarations are pinned by test. An adopter-edited workflow copy is outside this claim, exactly as SN-005 narrows it. Current carriers, recorded here while the row is undecomposed (no design or test row yet exists to hold the binding): the moment-to-tier table is docs/stack.ini [ci-tiers]; the pinning test is tests/test_ci_tier_declaration.py.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"The shipped workflow's trigger set and per-trigger tier match the declared moment-to-tier table, pinned by test; a workflow trigger absent from the table, or one invoking anything other than the documented harness entry point, is a finding; the declared OS x Python matrix cells appear in the shipped workflow; SR-019's acceptance cross-references this row rather than restating it.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"M\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-005\"]\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-152]\r\ntitle = \"Hosted CI verdict is the harness's own\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-008\", \"SN-005\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"TEST-ENGINEER\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"The hosted CI job verdict shall carry the harness's own exit for the declared bar — the job failing when the harness exits nonzero, with a step log naming each step's outcome and no silently skipped required step — as the declared backstop re-run behind the bypassable local hook floor.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-008 (a reader can believe a green) and SN-005. This is the second half of the honest-limit pair SR-019 states from the local side: a local floor is bypassable (git commit --no-verify), so no-unchecked-write-enters-governed-state rests on the verdict at the moment of the act PLUS a re-run of the same bar away from that bypass. Attributed to B-05, the delivered package, on the DESIGN-CONTROL reading, the same argument SR-151 carries: the shall constrains what the SHIPPED WORKFLOW declares — no continue-on-error, no conditional skip, the harness's own exit as the job's — and the system holds no authority over an external runner honouring it. STATED SO IT IS NOT READ AS DESIGN CONTROL OVER THE RUNNER: where hosted CI is configured, the re-run crosses at B-11, hosted CI (EXT-007) drawn as a party of its own, and this row still attaches to B-05 because the workflow is what the system ships and the runner honouring it is outside the system's control. SR-114 keeps the portability obligation; the CI matrix as an evidence surface is this row's.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"The shipped workflow contains no continue-on-error or conditional skip around a required harness step; a nonzero harness exit fails the job; the step log names the harness invocation and its tier. This row is the backstop half of the pair SR-019 states from the local side.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"M\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-005\"]\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-154]\r\ntitle = \"Independent review routed across families\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-026\", \"SN-024\", \"SN-006\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-09\", \"B-10\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]\r\nrequirement = \"The delivered loop content shall obtain, when unattended work reaches integration, each review or critique verdict the declared policy requires from a session that did not author the work — resolved per in-process phase and tier from the delivered agent registry's declared (family x model x tier) rows and only while the declared consent surface that turns managed selection on is present, drawn from a different model family wherever one is configured, degrading only to the documented same-family mode — with every selection logged before launch and a non-converging rework loop escalated through the declared approval level, and, where a claimed work item is marked for an in-lane single plan, refuse build output at its making or landing until a pass record binds its plan and Done-when.\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-026 (cross-family second opinions — every prior carrier of this contract demoted as routing machinery, so the sn_refs join forced the mint; SR-155 cites SN-026 too, for the planner pair, but only this row states the second opinion itself), SN-024 (an author cannot judge its own output) and SN-006. One row because routing, scheduling, scoring and escalation are one delivered contract — that the second opinion happens, independently, or its absence is documented — whose mechanics are the component details below it. The row also carries SN-026's DECLARATION and CONSENT half — `docs/agents.toml`'s pair-rows and the `docs/agents-enabled` surface whose presence turns managed selection on. That half had ZERO textual occurrence anywhere in the SR layer while `orphans=0` still held, because an orphan count proves a need has a citing row and never that the row carries the whole need. Managed selection is opt-in by consent rather than by configuration alone: a repository that declares families without dropping the surface has declared a capability, not turned one on, and the row now says so where a check can read it. fan-out re-stamp: the single plan's independent critique is one obligation carried by its briefs and filing and by its gate; the routing children remain separate.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"A declared review policy of N schedules N independent reviewer sessions; the declared (family x model x tier) pair-rows of the delivered agent registry are the only candidate source, and the declared consent surface's presence is what turns managed selection on — absent, managed selection is off and no row is resolved; present, exactly one row resolves per in-process phase and tier; a configured cross-family draw is preferred and its unavailability degrades to the documented mode, never a silent skip; every selection is logged before launch, never a silent model swap; rework iterates within the declared budget and pages per the declared approval level on exhaustion. The verdict that may clear integration comes from a session minted for that review, or, where reviewer retention is on and the declared final-reviewer setting selects persistence, from a round the coordinator recorded as final for the lane's retained final reviewer, over the whole lane, from its recorded claim to its reviewed tip; iteration rounds between full rounds review only rework since the last reviewed state, answer that round's findings, and never clear integration, whether their session was started fresh or resumed. Where a claimed work item is marked for an in-lane single plan, no build output is accepted at its making or landing until a pass record binds its plan and Done-when; the plan either covers every Done-when item or excludes it with a reason, declares an architectural delta of none, or one carried within its scope. One revision receives a fresh independent critique. If that second critique does not read as an approval, only an accepted dispute dismissal of every blocking or major finding permits the record; otherwise the item goes to the owner. A plan or Done-when changed after the record requires a fresh record. Ticking a Done-when item, or adding evidence to it, does not require a fresh record. Work items whose plan mark is absent, empty, none or dual are not held by this planning requirement; an unrecognized mark is held.\"\r\npriority = \"S\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 1\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-007\"]\r\naspect = \"unattended-loop\"\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-155]\r\ntitle = \"Contested planning rounds for marked work\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-024\", \"SN-006\", \"SN-026\", \"SN-002\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-01\", \"B-09\", \"B-10\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"Where work is declared as contested planning, the delivered loop content shall produce the selected decomposition through a bounded round of two independently authored rival plans — cross-critiqued, mechanically coverage-compared and arbitrated by fresh sessions — committing the selected outcome atomically as registry-valid queued rows and surfacing a non-converging round through the declared approval level, never falling back to a single uncontested plan silently.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"Realizes SN-024 (a decomposition judged by a competing plan and an independent arbiter rather than its author), with SN-026 (the planner pair prefers distinct families), SN-002 (the selected outcome lands as registry-valid rows, not prose) and SN-006. One row because the dual-plan round is one delivered capability with one observable outcome class (SELECT or PAGE); its state machine, briefs, adapters and isolation rules are the component tier's. Fan-out re-stamp: the round is one delivered capability with one observable outcome class, and its children are the successive phases of that single round — planner pair, briefs, coverage comparison, arbitration, isolation, disposition — none of which an adopter can obtain, refuse, or observe independently of the round, so the child count measures the round's step count rather than a merge of contracts.\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A row marked for contested planning is refused on the direct build path; the round runs planner pair, cross-critique, mechanical coverage comparison and position-swapped arbitration as fresh sessions within declared budgets; SELECT files children that pass the registry validator atomically; PAGE preserves the round's evidence and maps through the declared approval level.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"S\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 4\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-007\"]\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-156]\r\ntitle = \"Bounded lanes narrowing to one gated landing\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-027\", \"SN-008\", \"SN-025\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-01\", \"B-09\", \"B-10\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY\", \"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"The delivered loop content shall run exactly one work item per lane on bounded, mutually isolated lanes and narrow every lane back to the integration branch through one serial, fail-closed seam that runs the declared bar on the composed tree — parking a red candidate and stopping the queue loudly, draining claiming to a clean merged stop under a declared pause, and reconstructing claim and queue state from version-control history alone at any crash boundary, never a half-integrated authoritative state.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-027 WHOLE — ready work fans out across bounded parallel lanes and that fan-out narrows to one serialized gated seam before anything lands, in the need's own words — with SN-008 (the seam is fail-closed) and SN-025 (recovery from version-control history alone). ONE DECISION PER ROW: \"serial integration is one delivered contract\" is sound for the SEAM, but lane execution, claim authority and the trunk-side mint of work-item identity are not the seam, and a row stating the seam alone leaves SN-027's FIRST half — bounded lanes, isolated working trees, a worker ceiling — stated nowhere. This row therefore states the whole lane LIFECYCLE (claim, run isolated, close, land), which is what closes that hole; the trunk-only authority contract sheds to SR-170. The two fail independently: a perfectly serialized landing that lets a lane commit a regenerated artifact satisfies this row and not that one. Terminal close is SR-144's and is not restated here — one SR per (need, property), and both rows sit under SN-027 — so what this row carries of it is only that a terminal branch still lands through the one serial seam.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A launch with independent ready work runs up to the configured lane ceiling concurrently in isolated working trees, and a single-lane setting preserves the serial semantic; a finished branch reaches the integration branch only through the serial seam with the declared bar green on the composed tree — a red parks the candidate and stops the queue loudly; a declared pause stops claiming and drains in-flight lanes to a merged stop; a lane closed under the terminal-close contract (SR-144's, not restated here) reaches the integration branch through this same serial seam and by no other path; when a lane changes a claimed Done-when, its in-lane blessing binds the exact changed text before any subsequent build or rework dispatch, staged terminal close, or serial landing, while a review or adjudication session and the change's own commit remain unheld; a crash at any lifecycle boundary recovers from version-control history without double-assignment. A review-gated landing clears only from independent review sessions over the lane from its recorded claim base to the reviewed tip, each started fresh for that review or, where reviewer retention is on and the declared final-reviewer setting selects persistence, recorded by the coordinator as final for the lane's retained final reviewer; a partial-scope, iteration-round, invalid, absent, or dissenting review holds the landing, as does any other retained-session review.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"M\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 4\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-006\", \"DA-013\"]\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-157]\r\ntitle = \"Spine and work-registry rules red the harness verdict\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-002\", \"SN-012\", \"SN-025\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-09\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"FIRST-RUN-ADOPTER\", \"TEST-ENGINEER\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"The delivered harness shall report every declared spine and work-registry rule violation — broken joins, integrity and schema faults, leftover placeholders, requirement-form findings and work-item coherence contradictions — naming the at-fault row and cell, gating the declared failure set at the declared gate while advisory classes never change the exit code.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-002 (the chain is mechanically verified, not asserted — this row is the boundary-level home of the verdict SN-002's acceptance asks for), SN-012 (optional registries and opt-outs cost a non-user nothing) and SN-025 (the tracked work-item graph the loop derives its next work from is kept coherent). One row because the adopter-observable contract is one: registry rules produce named findings at a declared severity; which rules, at which severities, is the component detail the rows below it decompose. Deliberate pair (census F6): the PB-format invariant itself is SR-015's; this row's decomposition carries the checker. Fan-out re-stamp: the delivered contract is one — a named, row-and-cell-attributed finding at a declared severity, gating or advisory — while the rule inventory it ranges over is open by this row's own acceptance (\"a rule added at one of those sites is in this row's scope by default\"), so the child count tracks the number of declared rules rather than the number of decisions this row makes, and would climb back through any bound a split bought.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"Each declared registry rule violation is reported with row-level attribution; the declared strict set exits nonzero at its gate and advisory classes never join the exit code; absent or placeholder-only optional registries and declared opt-outs are vacuous; the declared verification vocabulary (including Critique) is accepted and an unknown value fails. The declaration this is read against is the rule inventory the delivered checkers themselves publish — the id shapes, the required cells and the closed vocabularies (with the interface and component entries advisory by their own recorded ruling), the strict flag families and their stated exit contracts, the gating form and provenance findings beside the never-gating paraphrase and acceptance advisories, and the work-item coherence rules with their declared opt-out — each recorded at its declaration site, not restated here. A rule added at one of those sites is in this row's scope by default: an unreported one is a finding against this row, not an amendment to it.\"\r\npriority = \"M\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 1\r\ncoincident = \"\"\"The needs ask for a chain that is mechanically verified rather than asserted, work-registry contradictions that surface rather than hide, and small changes kept cheap; each declared rule violation reported naming its row and cell, with the declared failure set gating and advisories not, is that verification's verdict as the reader receives it. Whether a row that passes every rule says something worth relying on is not this row's claim.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-158]\r\ntitle = \"Documentation drift reds or warns per its declared tier\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-010\", \"SN-008\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-09\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"CONSISTENCY\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"The delivered harness shall report a documentation surface that has drifted from what it claims — a broken intra-repo link, a missing vision declaration, a reference to an absent path or symbol, a stale generated doc, or a declared figure without its provenance — at the declared warn-or-gate severity for each class.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-010 (navigable, honest documentation) and SN-008 (a green never hides a stale claim). One row because the delivered contract is one honesty verdict over the documentation surfaces; the individual checkers and their carve-outs are component details.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"A dead intra-repo link, an absent or repeated vision declaration, a stale generated doc under the staleness check, a dangling backticked path or symbol reference, and a declared figure marker missing its command or revision each produce a finding at their declared tier; the declared carve-outs (generated blocks, per-line and per-file allow markers, unmarked figures, URLs and placeholders) stay silent. The declared tiering, read off each class's declaration site rather than restated: link and vision findings gate from the first requirements bar on; orphans and staleness warn by default, orphans gating only under their de