not an attestation. The commit that moved NOTHING is refused by that pairing rather than by a clause of its own: it names no source branch, and its empty id list composes a subject no real close carries. One property admits the two classes and it is not two rules: both are machine-authored end to end, and both move the tree without the lane having changed what it CLAIMS - docs/work/ is deliberately inside the identity because a spec's own claims are what a verdict is about, and the close carries those claims through unchanged. Every arm of both verifications fails toward REVIEW, since declining to peel measures at a later rev and can never ask for LESS - though not always for more: on the empty close the refused commit is identity-preserving, so the walk-through step reaches the same rev the peel would have, and the refusal guards this function's contract rather than any answer the gate gives. The two peels are NOT the same peel: work_tip calls refresh_attestation directly rather than through the shared disposable test, so a mechanical close is never removed by the destructive reset path, which may only ever drop a refresh sitting literally on the tip. governing_identity composes governing_rev and tree_identity for the branch tip or an explicit revision, including a round's reviewed commit and a trailer's carrier; the branch argument is a branch NAME, because the peel verifies a refresh commit against the branch it names and no refresh subject names HEAD. format_scope records a REVIEW session scope as full, narrow or final base..sha; gating_span admits a fresh full scope in either mode, or a final scope only where reviewer retention is on and final_reviewer is persisted; a narrow scope and a retained full scope never admit. logged_rounds joins branch-scoped round files to coordinator session logs by train and ordinal, and each round's review phase is the JOINED LOG's declared phase rather than the one its own filename carries, so a file cannot claim a phase its session did not serve; a joined key whose logs declare more than one review phase yields no round. It retains only a gating span whose base equals the caller's claim base and whose reviewed sha the round file names. round_entries retains only rounds whose reviewed revision governs the identity under judgement and emits phase, ordinal and verdict entries through an injected parser. filing_refusal applies one filing check: the first physical line is exactly the Reviewed full-sha opener (a CR ending is allowed; no leading blank or whitespace is), exactly one canonical VERDICT line, a finding count matching the file, and a change request naming a finding. An unreadable or refused round is an entry with no verdict, so it is the phase's latest word rather than an older verdict being used. tree_already_judged is true only for an entry carrying a verdict and false with no base. declared_phases clamps the configured independent-review count to the available review phases. phases_owed returns declared phases whose latest entry is missing or invalid evidence; a dissent is served. round_count returns the largest per-phase entry count at one governing identity, so a multi-phase review cycle counts once and changed work starts a new count. format_trailer and parse_trailer carry `Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>`. branch_trailers verifies each carrier against its governing identity and returns the ordered attestation sequence per tree. Readers treat unavailable repository answers according to their own fail-closed contract.\"\"\"\r\n+method = \"\"\"Drive the real worker loop as a subprocess against a fake agent CLI in throwaway git repos, from explicit --wi/--train assignments and from --wi alone, whose session tag defaults to the branch name. Assert the composed prompt carries the WI row, its SpecRef, its predecessor context, the branch diff of an earlier assigned row and the trailer protocol, forbids resuming from docs/status.md, and carries the con